 ],
 "says": "The founder founds Team A for review with Bora as reviewer; Bora accepts the exact founding request and it commits with a grant for each of them. Under Team A the founder commits a source (source.revision.commit) and sets that source's own rights to allow read, use and derive (source.rights.set). The founder then founds a new Team by derivation (team.found, self-founded, with derived_from naming Team A and selecting exactly two things: the source's stored revision and Team A's policy as its settings). The proposal carries its own new team_id. The owner commits the copy under its own head with its own policy, one grant for the founder, an active state and a profile named Platform copy. A team.state.read of the copy returns exactly those: no membership, no grant for Bora, no approval, no credential and none of Team A's history. A read of Team A at its head still returns Team A's two grants and state, so the derivation did not change the original.",
 "spec_sha256": "a144a3a233250f3172f2dc92fcb12fca2a937d1bf29b7b8d3c396994cdd0d81b",
